00:10:27,516 --> 00:10:28,555
falling.

294
00:10:28,817 --> 00:10:30,867
Let me draw the cycle.

295
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:33,019
Costs rise faster than prices,

296
00:10:33,019 --> 00:10:35,437
and insurers lose money.

297
00:10:35,547 --> 00:10:37,392
Insurers raise prices,

298
00:10:37,392 --> 00:10:38,527
sharply.

299
00:10:38,607 --> 00:10:39,714
Costs cool down,

300
00:10:39,714 --> 00:10:42,241
but prices are already high,

301
00:10:42,241 --> 00:10:43,977
and profits soar.

302
00:10:44,177 --> 00:10:46,817
Then competition and regulators push

303
00:10:46,817 --> 00:10:48,377
prices back down.

304
00:10:48,467 --> 00:10:51,044
Drivers live through the expensive part of

305
00:10:51,044 --> 00:10:52,674
every turn.

306
00:10:52,917 --> 00:10:55,188
So why did your car insurance get

307
00:10:55,188 --> 00:10:56,797
so expensive?

308
00:10:56,927 --> 00:10:59,153
More expensive cars and repairs,

309
00:10:59,153 --> 00:11:00,379
deadlier crashes,

310
00:11:00,379 --> 00:11:02,855
rising legal and medical costs,

311
00:11:02,855 --> 00:11:05,606
and insurers who raised prices fast to

312
00:11:05,606 --> 00:11:07,707
make up for their losses.

313
00:11:07,747 --> 00:11:10,177
Prices are finally easing.

314
00:11:10,227 --> 00:11:12,220
But they remain far above where they

315
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:13,970
were before the pandemic,

316
00:11:13,970 --> 00:11:15,742
and the next turn of the cycle

317
00:11:15,742 --> 00:11:17,671
is never far away.

318
00:11:17,917 --> 00:11:20,001
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

319
00:11:20,001 --> 00:11:22,487
we follow the money behind another hidden

320
00:11:22,487 --> 00:11:24,617
link of the world economy.

321
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,693
This is The Hidden Economics.
